meta {
  name: Phase 2 - Schedule Counseling
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/college-admin/seat-cancellations/{{seatCancellationId}}/schedule-counseling
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{staffToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "counselor_id": "{{staffMemberId}}",
    "scheduled_at": "2026-10-14T10:30:00"
  }
}

docs {
  Assigns a college-admin staff member (the "counselor" — no separate
  identity table, any active StaffMember at this college can be assigned;
  404 if the id isn't a staff member at this college) and the scheduled
  date/time for the mandatory exit counseling session. Advances the case
  from Phase 2 to Phase 3 immediately (this records the schedule
  confirmation, not that the session itself has already happened).

  Also creates a real Google Meet event (via the same Calendar/Meet
  integration the Interview module uses — GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID/SECRET,
  GOOGLE_MEET_REFRESH_TOKEN, GOOGLE_MEET_CALENDAR_ID) — a 30-minute session
  starting at scheduled_at, with the counselor's and student's email as
  attendees (whichever are available). This is best-effort: if Meet isn't
  configured or the API call fails, scheduling still succeeds and
  meetingUrl stays null on the response — never blocks the phase advance.

  Response includes meetingUrl (the generated Meet link) — also surfaced on
  the student-facing GET /student/seat-cancellations list.

  409 ConflictError if the case isn't currently at Phase 2.
}
